{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"82f9042bd9037f99","type":"text","text":"Yeh tools cybersecurity me alag-alag kaam ke liye use hote hain. Sirf apne systems, labs, ya authorized security testing me hi use karein.\n\n|Tool|Kis liye use hota hai|Example Use|\n|---|---|---|\n|**Hydra**|Login/password authentication ki security test karna|SSH, FTP, HTTP login ki authorized password testing|\n|**John the Ripper**|Password hash recovery (CPU-based)|Linux shadow hash ya password audit|\n|**Hashcat**|GPU-based password hash recovery|Large wordlists aur rule-based password audits|\n|**SQLMap**|SQL Injection vulnerabilities detect aur verify karna|Web application database security testing|\n|**Nmap**|Network scanning aur service discovery|Open ports, running services, OS detection|\n|**Dirb**|Hidden directories/files discover karna|`/admin`, `/backup`, `/uploads` jaise paths dhoondhna|\n|**cURL**|HTTP/HTTPS requests bhejna aur APIs test karna|GET, POST requests, headers, downloads|\n|**Netcat (nc)**|TCP/UDP connections, data transfer aur troubleshooting|Port connectivity test, simple client/server communication|\n|**CeWL**|Website se custom wordlist banana|Company/site ke words collect karke password audit ke liye custom dictionary banana|\n|**Crunch**|Pattern ke hisaab se custom wordlists generate karna|Jaise `Name123`, PIN patterns, ya fixed-length combinations|\n|**tmux**|Terminal multiplexer|Multiple terminal sessions ek hi window me chalana, sessions ko resume karna|\n\n### Ek typical authorized penetration testing workflow\n\n| Step                         | Tool                      |\n| ---------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Network scan                 | Nmap                      |\n| Web content discovery        | Dirb                      |\n| HTTP/API testing             | cURL                      |\n| SQL Injection testing        | SQLMap                    |\n| Custom wordlist              | CeWL                      |\n| Pattern-based wordlist       | Crunch                    |\n| Password hash audit          | John the Ripper / Hashcat |\n| Terminal session management  | tmux                      |\n| Network connectivity testing | Netcat                    |\n\n### Yaad rakhne ki trick\n\n- [x] 🌐 **Nmap** → Network scan\n- [x] 📂 **Dirb** → Directories search\n- [ ] 🌍 **cURL** → Web/API requests\n- [ ] 🗄️ **SQLMap** → SQL Injection testing\n- [x] 🔑 **John** → Password hash recovery (CPU)\n- [x] ⚡ **Hashcat** → Password hash recovery (GPU)\n- [x] 📝 **CeWL** → Website se wordlist\n- [x] 🔤 **Crunch** → Custom wordlist generation\n- [ ] 🖥️ **tmux** → Terminal management\n- [ ] 🔌 **Netcat** → Network connections & debugging\n- [x] 🔐 **Hydra** → Login authentication security testing","x":-386,"y":-263,"width":1212,"height":1143},
		{"id":"dbf6b9b1aafd548f","type":"file","file":"Cyber Security Practically/Tools/screenshots/wordlist.png","x":-385,"y":940,"width":605,"height":323},
		{"id":"28408261c6d17f1b","type":"text","text":"`Patator Tools` for Bruteforce on protocol like smb ssh telnet smnp","x":-385,"y":1340,"width":530,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"241b478edd16577e","type":"text","text":"Medusa for host Bruteforce","x":-386,"y":1440,"width":366,"height":60},
		{"id":"8017c19134856ad7","type":"text","text":"```\n$ medusa\nMedusa v2.3 [http://www.foofus.net] (C) JoMo-Kun / Foofus Networks <jmk@foofus.net>\n\nALERT: Host information must be supplied.\n\nSyntax: Medusa [-h host|-H file] [-u username|-U file] [-p password|-P file] [-C file] -M module [OPT]\n  -h [TEXT]    : Target hostname or IP address\n  -H [FILE]    : File containing target hostnames or IP addresses\n  -u [TEXT]    : Username to test\n  -U [FILE]    : File containing usernames to test\n  -p [TEXT]    : Password to test\n  -P [FILE]    : File containing passwords to test\n  -C [FILE]    : File containing combo entries. See README for more information.\n  -O [FILE]    : File to append log information to\n  -e [n/s/ns]  : Additional password checks ([n] No Password, [s] Password = Username)\n  -M [TEXT]    : Name of the module to execute (without the .mod extension)\n  -m [TEXT]    : Parameter to pass to the module. This can be passed multiple times with a\n                 different parameter each time and they will all be sent to the module (i.e.\n                 -m Param1 -m Param2, etc.)\n  -d           : Dump all known modules\n  -n [NUM]     : Use for non-default TCP port number\n  -s           : Enable SSL\n  -g [NUM]     : Give up after trying to connect for NUM seconds (default 3)\n  -r [NUM]     : Sleep NUM seconds between retry attempts (default 3)\n  -R [NUM]     : Attempt NUM retries before giving up. The total number of attempts will be NUM + 1.\n  -c [NUM]     : Time to wait in usec to verify socket is available (default 500 usec).\n  -t [NUM]     : Total number of logins to be tested concurrently\n  -T [NUM]     : Total number of hosts to be tested concurrently\n  -L           : Parallelize logins using one username per thread. The default is to process \n                 the entire username before proceeding.\n  -f           : Stop scanning host after first valid username/password found.\n  -F           : Stop audit after first valid username/password found on any host.\n  -b           : Suppress startup banner\n  -q           : Display module's usage information\n  -v [NUM]     : Verbose level [0 - 6 (more)]\n  -w [NUM]     : Error debug level [0 - 10 (more)]\n  -V           : Display version\n  -Z [TEXT]    : Resume scan based on map of previous scan\n```","x":-386,"y":1580,"width":886,"height":978},
		{"id":"6625e768178f5270","type":"text","text":"Same on `nccrack`","x":220,"y":1340,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
